    "title": "Promoter KPIs & Performance Evaluation",
    "lastUpdated": "2026-09-01",
    "source": "DAY 1 Training Deck v2.4 + Promoter KPI Update, effective Sept 1, 2026",
    "body": "\n    <p>Current minimum monthly targets that determine bonus eligibility (see also\n    <a href=\"#incentive-formula\">Incentive Formula</a> and the <a href=\"#changelog\">Change Log</a> for how this\n    number evolved):</p>\n    <ul>\n      <li>2 applications per day (≈60/month)</li>\n      <li><strong>27 booked applications/month</strong> — note may flex by store performance</li>\n      <li><strong>₱320,000 in Sales Volume (Financed Amount)</strong> per month</li>\n      <li>₱13,200 Average Financed Amount (AFA)</li>\n      <li><strong>80% VAS Penetration Rate</strong> (raised from 75%, effective Sept 1, 2026)</li>\n      <li>Risk below 12% (FSTPD30)</li>\n      <li>Positive TSM Evaluation</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h4>Performance Evaluation weighting (basis for regularization)</h4>\n    <table>\n      <tr><th>KPI</th><th>Weight</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>Applications per month</td><td>10%</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Booked SIL per month</td><td>35%</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Financed Amount</td><td>10%</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>VAS Penetration Rate</td><td>10%</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Risk Performance (FSTPD30)</td><td>35%</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <h4>Risk KPI Assessment Scale (FSTPD30 → KPI fulfillment)</h4>\n    <table>\n      <tr><th>Budgeted FSTPD30</th><th>KPI Fulfillment</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>&gt;12%</td><td>0%</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>11.01–12%</td><td>50%</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>10.01–11%</td><td>80%</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>7.01–10%</td><td>90%</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>&lt;7%</td><td>100%</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <p>A mandatory coaching session with the TSM follows every performance evaluation, especially for anyone who\n    missed target. <strong>Low Performing for 2 consecutive months</strong> → TSM decides on End of Contract (EOC)\n    or one more chance. <strong>Low Performing for 3 consecutive months</strong> → PHI issues a Notice of End of\n    Employment.</p>\n  ",
    "titleTL": "Mga KPI ng Promoter & Performance Evaluation",
    "bodyTL": "\n      <p>Kasalukuyang minimum monthly targets na nagtatakda kung eligible ka para sa bonus (tingnan din\n      ang <a href=\"#incentive-formula\">Incentive Formula</a> at ang <a href=\"#changelog\">Change Log</a> para sa kasaysayan ng numerong ito):</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li>2 applications kada araw (≈60/buwan)</li>\n        <li><strong>27 booked applications/buwan</strong> — puwedeng mag-iba depende sa performance ng store</li>\n        <li><strong>₱320,000 sa Sales Volume (Financed Amount)</strong> kada buwan</li>\n        <li>₱13,200 Average Financed Amount (AFA)</li>\n        <li>75% VAS Penetration Rate</li>\n        <li>Risk na mas mababa sa 12% (FSTPD30)</li>\n        <li>Positibong TSM Evaluation</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h4>Timbang ng Performance Evaluation (basehan ng regularization)</h4>\n      <table>\n        <tr><th>KPI</th><th>Weight</th></tr>\n        <tr><td>Applications per month</td><td>10%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Booked SIL per month</td><td>35%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Financed Amount</td><td>10%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>VAS Penetration Rate</td><td>10%</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Risk Performance (FSTPD30)</td><td>35%</td></tr>\n      </table>\n      <p>May mandatory coaching session kasama ang TSM pagkatapos ng bawat performance evaluation, lalo na sa mga hindi umabot sa target.\n      <strong>Low Performing sa 2 magkasunod na buwan</strong> → magdedesisyon ang TSM kung End of Contract (EOC) o bibigyan pa ng isa pang tsansa.\n      <strong>Low Performing sa 3 magkasunod na buwan</strong> → maglalabas ang PHI ng Notice of End of Employment.</p>\n    ",
    "flags": [
      "VAS Penetration Rate target raised from 75% to 80%, effective Sept 1, 2026."
    ]
