    "source": "DAY 1 Training Deck v2.4",
    "body": "\n    <ul>\n      <li>Onboarding is a <strong>two-day training</strong>. Every trainee is still an <em>applicant</em> until they pass.</li>\n      <li>An <strong>end-of-day exam</strong> follows each day. <strong>Passing score: 80%.</strong> Exams are randomized.</li>\n      <li>Only after passing both exams does a trainee receive a Job Order (JO), then a contract.</li>\n      <li>Integrity is strictly enforced — any infraction against integrity or professionalism during training results in immediate dismissal from the class.</li>\n      <li>Store assignment speed depends on store availability in the area and how quickly pre-employment documents are completed.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h4>Reapplication conditions</h4>\n    <table>\n      <tr><th>Situation</th><th>Can reapply after</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>No-show on Final Interview or Training</td><td>1 year</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Failed the exams</td><td>6 months (repeat full process)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Resigned Purple Pro</td><td>Case-by-case — must ask PHI, depends on reason for leaving</td></tr>\n    </table>\n  "
